Z||000013||Kelvin Vivian||12-15-2001||01:26 AM||||Nice daily driver, 85 SE V6s are neat because they are the only model Fiero that has the "original" Fiero body with a V6 engine.  It's the sleeper Fiero model.<P>Here's pics of my current daily driver, an 87 SE - looks like an 85 GT, even has the dual factory exhausts, but mechanically identical to an 87 4-cyl coupe.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"> This is the opposite of a sleeper Fiero model, but the 4-cyl does have some torque in her.<P>1987 SE 4-cyl, 5-spd<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.printroom.com/_vti_bin/ViewImage.dll?userid=no_18&album_id=36084&image_id=0&courtesy=1"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.printroom.com/_vti_bin/ViewImage.dll?userid=no_18&album_id=36084&image_id=1&courtesy=1"> ||||reg||14
